00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.560
- And now, here's something neat

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.780
that I wanted you all to see.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.400
Take a look.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.350
- Hi, Drew, it's Liz of Eat Cake Be Merry

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.250
and I wanna share with you

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.950
how to create these
adorable puppy cupcakes.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.450
First, you'll want to shape some fondant

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.530
to create the ears, eyes, tongue and nose.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.250
Then color some buttercream and
place them into piping bags.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.770
Now grab a cupcake, and using a grass tip,

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.650
pipe lines that extend
from the center out.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.540
Go ahead and cover the entire surface

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.580
of the cupcake with fur.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.780
Once you've done that,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.543
let's create some of the
puppy's facial features.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.220
Now you can add both ears,
angle them just a little,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.220
two eyes, a cute nose, and
of course, a pink tongue.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.173
Let's add some twinkle to
those precious puppy eyes.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.463
So adorable. Isn't it just the cutest?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.953
Let's bring in some friends.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.930
There you have a fun and easy way

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.660
to create the cutest cupcakes.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.820
- Hi, Drew, it's Pati Jinich.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.430
To help celebrate Hispanic Heritage Month,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.350
I'm gonna make a salsa matcha,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.320
and it's gorgeous and so delicious.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.917
It's from my upcoming book,

00:01:14.917 --> 00:01:16.710
"Treasures of the Mexican Table."

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.310
And to make it, all you
need is five minutes

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.440
and you can use it in so many ways.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.250
So I'm gonna add olive oil, vegetable oil.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.570
Once it's hot, add walnuts,
pine nuts, pistachios,

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.740
garlic cloves, ancho chiles,
stem them, seed them,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.670
cut them into small pieces,
and chiles de arbol.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.020
So you're gonna stem them.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.173
I'm gonna keep the seeds,
and then I'm gonna stir.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.730
Add pumpkin seeds,
amaranth seeds, vinegar,

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.070
dark brown sugar, salt.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.280
Mix these up, and we're gonna let it cool.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.550
You can spoon it on top of avocado toast.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.330
You can spoon it on top
of pancakes, French toast.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.240
You can spoon it on top of yogurt, fruit.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.560
You can eat it in so many ways.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.483
It's super yum.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.230
- Hi Drew, I'm Capri Lily,
creator of Good Food Baddie.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.640
And today I'll be showing you how to make

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.580
these spooky pumpkin ice
cream cookie sandwiches.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.060
Here I have homemade double
chocolate chip cookies

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.740
and they're gonna serve as the base

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.110
for our pumpkin ice
cream cookie sandwiches.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.000
Right now, I'm gonna show you how to make

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.610
your own pumpkin ice cream at home.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.670
I'm gonna start off by
adding the pumpkin puree.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.480
Then I'll add coconut cream,
maple syrup, pumpkin spice,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.510
cinnamon, coconut sugar,
and blend until it's smooth.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.770
Then I'll place it in the bread pan

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.050
and place it in the freezer for two hours.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.300
And now I have this delicious, smooth,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.730
creamy pumpkin spice ice cream.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.290
Now we'll take a scoop of the ice cream

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.760
and place it on top of our
double chocolate chip cookies

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.370
and then use another cookie

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.410
to finish and complete the sandwich.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.400
And we're all done.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.260
We have these spooky pumpkin spice

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.724
ice cream cookie sandwiches.

00:03:03.724 --> 00:03:06.307
(upbeat music)

